  "abstract_html": "<p>For every torus knot, the rank of the differential of the Daemi–Scaduto S-complex of singular instanton homology is determined by the signature and the Alexander polynomial; this follows from theorems of Li–Ye and Daemi–Scaduto. For the torus knots <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(3,n)</annotation></semantics></math> the differential has rank zero or one according to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6</annotation></semantics></math>, and its rank equals Daemi and Scaduto’s Frøyshov-type invariant; they proved this in two of the four residue classes and for <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=4,5</annotation></semantics></math>, and Hedden, Herald and Kirk computed it for <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>38</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\le38</annotation></semantics></math>. Following Lewallen, Klassen and Hedden–Herald–Kirk, we describe the generators of the instanton complexes and their <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">ℤ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{Z}/4</annotation></semantics></math> gradings for two-bridge knots, whose irreducible traceless characters are all binary dihedral, and for <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(3,n)</annotation></semantics></math>, where at most one is. We also give a proof through Khovanov homology, using Schütz’s computation for three-braids, of Li and Ye’s computation of the rank of the instanton homology of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(3,n)</annotation></semantics></math>, and compare the differential of the knot <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mn>8</mn><mn>19</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">8_{19}</annotation></semantics></math> with the single pillowcase bigon of Hedden, Herald and Kirk.</p>",
